The attached image, Figure 9, demonstrates that Nano-11 enhances the antibody response to adsorbed antigens. Mice immunized with recombinant protective antigen (rPA) formulated with Nano-11, at doses of 50 µg, 200 µg, and 800 µg/dose, developed significantly higher anti-rPA IgG titers compared to soluble rPA alone (p < 0.01). The immune response induced by Nano-11 was comparable to, or in some cases exceeded, that achieved with aluminum hydroxide adjuvant. This indicates Nano-11's effectiveness as a vaccine adjuvant in strongly enhancing antigen-specific humoral immunity in vivo.